NO ADVICE, AND A SPECIFIC CAUTION

This is a research method. It is not investment advice, legal advice, tax
advice, or financial advice, and it is not a substitute for professional
counsel or your own diligence.

It runs on large language models, which make mistakes. It is deliberately built
to state its confidence, disclose what it could not verify, and label
constructed figures as constructed, so you can see where it is uncertain. Read
those sections. Verify anything you intend to act on, especially figures that
carry money.

Do not commit capital on the strength of a document this method produced. Use
it to decide what is worth checking, then check it.


